    "limits": [
      "No FIFO or indefinite fairness guarantee; acquisition can return conflict after 15 seconds of contention",
      "Lease expiry permits takeover and prevents starting a new local publication; it does not cancel an already-submitted ClickHouse transaction",
      "A timed-out or aborted in-flight request may finish if neither takeover nor cleanup has fenced it; the delayed-publication test observes this behavior explicitly",
      "Cancellation cleanup is best effort and bounded; storage outage or an acquisition that finishes after cleanup may require lease expiry for recovery",
      "The acquisition timeout and remaining-lease commit timeout do not establish a global end-to-end operation latency bound"
